        "correct": false,
        "why": "There are no such routes."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-4p6q7f0n",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "first-app",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "Why does the API run on port 8001?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "To leave 8000 to Django",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right: the two never fight over a port, which only one server may hold."
      },
      {
        "text": "Uvicorn refuses port 8000",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "It accepts any free port."
      },
      {
        "text": "FastAPI requires an odd port",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "There is no such rule."
      },
      {
        "text": "8001 is the ASGI standard port",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "ASGI has no standard port."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-zx818bag",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "first-app",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "The first list_events returned dictionaries with datetime values. How did they become JSON?",
    "hint": "Nobody wrote a serializer.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "json.dumps, which handles datetime",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "json.dumps refuses datetime objects."
      },
      {
        "text": "Uvicorn converted them",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "Uvicorn sends bytes it is given."
      },
      {
        "text": "FastAPI's jsonable_encoder",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right: ISO 8601 strings with their offset."
      },
      {
        "text": "The store kept them as strings",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "store.py builds datetime objects."
      }
    ]
  },
